# What the Java generator writes that this repository does not want.
#
# See the Python ignore file for the reasoning; the same two kinds of line appear
# here.
#
# The hand-written helper — src/main/java/com/applab/sdk/AppLabExt.java — is
# listed so regeneration never touches it. The generator does not produce it, but
# listing it is what keeps it safe if a future generator version decides to, and
# it records that the file is ours rather than the tool's.
#
# pom.xml and the generated runtime (ApiClient.java, apis/, models/) are NOT
# listed: they are what makes the SDK compile, which is the point of shipping it.

# Ours, protected from regeneration.
src/main/java/com/applab/sdk/AppLabExt.java

# CI and publishing for a standalone project; this SDK lives inside AppLab.
.github/
git_push.sh
.travis.yml
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Documentation and tests the generator emits alongside the code.
docs/
src/test/

# The repository's own ignore rules are managed at the root.
# The generator's copy would be a second set that silently disagrees.
.gitignore
